## Required: Load at Session Start

At the start of every session, you MUST:
1. Read `AGENTS.md` — single source of truth for all rules, roles, and workflows.
2. Read the hot files `memory-bank/activeContext.md` + `memory-bank/progress.md` (every session); if mem0 is configured, search shared memory; read the 4 foundation files on first contact, after >=2 weeks away, or for architecture-touching tasks (see skills/memory-bank-protocol.md):
   (foundation files: projectbrief.md → productContext.md → systemPatterns.md → techContext.md)
3. Read `manifest.yaml` — project registry; clone any missing repos listed there.
4. Read `skills/INDEX.md` — full skill catalog with trigger conditions.

These reads are non-optional.

## Skill Invocation Rule

When any skill is triggered, read the full skill file (`skills/<name>.md`) before executing any steps.

## Skill Triggers

| Skill | Trigger |
|---|---|
| `write-tests.md` | Any new feature, bug fix, or refactor — before writing production code |
| `debug-investigation.md` | Bug report, unexpected behavior, or "fix" without clear diagnosis |
| `performance-profiling.md` | "slow", "latency", "timeout", "optimize", or monitoring p95/p99 spikes |
| `feature-flag-lifecycle.md` | Creating, rolling out, or graduating a feature flag |
| `plan-code-review-workflow.md` | Any non-trivial task (>1 file or user-facing impact) |
| `expert-pr-review.md` | Any PR review request |
| `triage-review-feedback.md` | Review feedback received on a PR WE authored (human, AI, or scanner); tags every FIX NEW/REPEAT |
| `pr-shepherd.md` | Start of day, PR status, "what's blocked?", after opening/un-drafting a PR |
| `reply-contract.md` | Status, "your turn", smoke / tap-through, anything the human must do |
| `codebase-simplification-audit.md` | Whole-repo read-only audit of data/state/ownership; no edits until user accepts a rec |
| `grill-with-docs.md` | Align on a plan/design before code; CONTEXT.md glossary; no implement until they confirm |
| `end-of-day-review.md` | End of working day, "wrap up", "plan tomorrow" |
| `multi-harness-coordination.md` | Coordinating work across two or more agent harnesses |
| `task-loop-7-phase.md` | 7-Phase Algorithm, TaskLoopState, observe/think/plan/build/execute/verify/learn |
| `cherry-pick-to-release-branch.md` | Hotfix or backport to a release branch |
| `memory-bank-protocol.md` | Session start, project switch, new project setup |
| `docs-protocol.md` | Creating or updating technical docs or ADRs |
| `subagent-routing.md` | Independent subtasks, parallelizable work, model selection |
| `delegation-patterns.md` | Multi-agent delegation with worktree isolation |
| `black-box-agent-qa.md` | Before treating any agent, harness, verb, or skill change as tested/passing/ready to ship; required by `close-out` Step 9 before a skill goes live |

## Global Rules (Summary)

- Absolute paths for all file operations.
- Never commit or push unless explicitly instructed.
- Confirm before deletions or destructive changes.
- TDD mandatory: failing test before production code (`docs/shared/tdd-standard.md`).
- Update `memory-bank/activeContext.md` and `progress.md` at end of every task.
- Evidence rule: status claims must cite SHA/PR/log.

See `AGENTS.md` for complete ruleset and role definitions.
